    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d210">

                <pb facs="0276" n="268" xml:id="pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/1788: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-15T19:00:00-05:00">December 15, 1941—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 16—7:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>538. Referring to Department’s telegram of December 13, 8 p.m., No. 387.<anchor
                        n="29" xml:id="d210-f1"/> In a preliminary informal conversation with the
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs this afternoon, he expressed his willingness to
                    conclude an agreement along the lines of the Department’s telegram. I am
                    [sending?] him a note<anchor n="30" xml:id="d210-f2"/> embodying the provisions
                    of the agreement tomorrow morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d210-f1" n="29" xml:id="d210-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, as telegram No. 228 to
                    the Minister in Guatemala, printed in <ref target="frus1941v06#pg_56">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">vi</hi>, p. 56</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d210-f2" n="30" xml:id="d210-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
